$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General method for the preparation of
1,2,3-triazoles (3a-3r) To a stirred solution of substituted benzyl
bromide (1 mmol), sodium azide (2.5 mmol), and bisalkynes (0.5 mmol) in
DMF/water (9:1) was added copper sulfate (5 mol%) and sodium ascorbate
(10 mol%). The reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for
6-12 h and the progress was monitored by TLC. Upon completion of the
reaction ice-cold water (30 ml) was added to the reaction mixture,
precipitates were collected by filtration and washed with aqueous ammonia
solution followed by water. To remove traces of reactant, precipitates
were further washed with ethyl acetate and dried under vacuum. Pure
product.
N1,N3-bis((1-(2-Methylbenzyl)-1H-1,2,3-triazol-4-yl)methyl)isophthalamide
(3a) N1
,N4-bis((1-(3-Methylbenzyl)-1H-1,2,3-triazol-4-yl)methyl)terephthalamide
(3h) Yield: 80 %; White solid; Mp: 189-190°C; IR (KBr): 3332 (N-H str),
3138 (=C-H str triazole), 3066, 2941, 1641, 1541, 1292, 1049 cm-1. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ 2.37 (s, 6H, CH3), 4.65 (s, 4H, NHCH2), 5.47 (s,
4H, NCH2), 7.07-7.14 (m, 4H, Ar-H), 7.21-7.25 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 7.75-7.82
(m, 2H, Ar-H), 7.93-7.94 (m, 6H, Ar-H + triazole), 8.91 (brs, 2H, NH,
exchangeable with D2O). 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ 20.6 (CH3), 35.2
(NHCH2), 53.4 (NCH2), 122.5 (C-5 triazole), 124.4 (C-6'), 127.2 (C-2,
C-3, C-5, C-6), 128.5 (C-4'), 128.3 (C-5'), 128.8 (C-2'), 136.5 (C-1,
C-4, C-1'), 138.2 (C-3'), 145.2 (C-4 triazole), 166.1 (C=O). HRMS: m/z
(M+) Cacld. for C30H30N8O2: 534.2492, found: 535.2563 (M+H)+.
