$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General method for the preparation of 1,2,3-triazoles (3a-3r) To a
stirred solution of substituted benzyl bromide (1 mmol), sodium azide
(2.5 mmol), and bisalkynes (0.5 mmol) in DMF/water (9:1) was added copper
sulfate (5 mol%) and sodium ascorbate (10 mol%). The reaction mixture was
stirred at ambient temperature for 6-12 h and the progress was monitored
by TLC. Upon completion of the reaction ice-cold water (30 ml) was added
to the reaction mixture, precipitates were collected by filtration and
washed with aqueous ammonia solution followed by water. To remove traces
of reactant, precipitates were further washed with ethyl acetate and
dried under vacuum. Pure product.
N1,N3-bis((1-(2-Methylbenzyl)-1H-1,2,3-triazol-4-yl)methyl)isophthalamide
(3a) Yield: 77 %; White solid; Mp: 162-164°C. IR (KBr): 3314 (N-H str),
3134 (=C-H str triazole), 3067, 2957, 1653, 1576, 1545, 1287, 1051, cm-1.
1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ 2.20 (s, 6H, CH3), 4.52 (s, 4H, NHCH2),
5.52 (s, 4H, NCH2), 7.14-7.25 (m, 8H, Ar-H), 7.56 (brs, 1H, Ar-H),
7.98-8.02 (m, 4H, Ar-H + triazole), 8.35 (s, 1H, Ar-H), 9.11 (brs, 2H,
NH, exchangeable with D2O). 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ 21.1 (CH3),
35.0 (NHCH2), 52.9 (NCH2), 123.2 (C-5 triazole), 125.3 (C-2), 126.6
(C-4'), 128.6 (C-5'), 128.7 (C-6'), 128.8 (C-5), 128.9 (C-3'), 130.1
(C-4, C-6), 134.4 (C-1, C-3), 136.1 (C-2'), 138.1C-1'), 145.3 (C-4
triazole), 165.9 (C=O). HRMS: m/z (M+) Cacld. for C30H30N8O2: 534.2492,
found: 535.2562 (M+H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, click reaction
